## <%if .DisplayName%><%.DisplayName%><%else%><%.Slug%><%end%> — shape: async questions (ADR-081).
##
## The drafting agent declares `interaction: async`: it posts the
## questions only the operator can answer with `ask_user_async` and
## KEEPS WORKING — answers arrive in its conversation whenever the
## operator replies (studio question cards, or `iterion runs answer`).
## The tools reach every backend: claude_code through iterion's ask-user
## MCP server, claw in-process, pi through its extension (ADR-081).
## The `await_answers` node is the DETERMINISTIC sync point: the run
## parks there, and only there, until every posted question is answered
## (mandatory timeout), then the finalizer resolves the placeholders.
## Fill in: the mission. docs/async-interaction.md

dsl: 2

<%template "vars_block" .%>
schema draft_out:
  draft: string

schema final_out:
  result: string

prompt mission:
<%indent 2 .Instructions%>

prompt draft_user:
  FIRST, post every question only the operator can answer, one
  ask_user_async call each. Then do everything that does not depend on
  the answers, incorporating any answer that arrives while you work.
  Return your draft with <PLACEHOLDER> marks where an unanswered detail
  belongs; call await_answers only if you have literally nothing left to
  do without the answers.

prompt final_user:
  ## Draft
  {{outputs.draft.draft}}

  ## Operator answers
  ```
  {{outputs.gate.answers}}
  ```
  Resolve every placeholder and return the final result.

## The working set is DECLARED here because `interaction:` grants the
## ask tools by adding them to this list — and on claw a non-empty list
## is the node's whole toolset. Left empty, the grant turns "no
## restriction" into exactly {ask_user, ask_user_async, await_answers,
## todo_write}: the agent could ask, and nothing else. Widen it for what
## your mission needs (`web_fetch`, an `mcp.<server>.*`).
agent draft:<%template "llm_fields" .%>
  interaction: async
  tools: [bash, read_file, write_file, file_edit, glob, grep, todo_write, skill]
  system: mission
  user: draft_user
  output: draft_out

## Blocks HERE (and only here) until every question the draft agent
## posted is answered. The timeout is mandatory: no silent infinity.
await_answers gate:
  from: draft
  timeout: "30m"

agent finalize:<%template "llm_fields" .%>
  system: mission
  user: final_user
  output: final_out

workflow <%.WorkflowName%>:
  entry: draft<%template "worktree_dial" .%><%template "dials" .%><%template "budget_block" .%>
  draft -> gate
  gate -> finalize
  finalize -> done
